{"parentUuid":"b2baf5a2-dcf6-47c1-91b4-9c38844fe57b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"agent_listing_delta","addedTypes":["claude","claude-code-guide","Explore","general-purpose","Plan","statusline-setup"],"addedLines":["- claude: Catch-all for any task that doesn't fit a more specific agent. FleetView's default when no agent name is typed. (Tools: *)","- claude-code-guide: Use this agent when the user asks questions (\"Can Claude...\", \"Does Claude...\", \"How do I...\") about: (1) Claude Code (the CLI tool) - features, hooks, slash commands, MCP servers, settings, IDE integrations, keyboard shortcuts; (2) Claude Agent SDK - building custom agents; (3) Claude API (formerly Anthropic API) - Messages API for directly passing messages to Claude, Tool Runner (`client.beta.messages.tool_runner`) for running an agentic loop over your own tools, manual tool-use loops, Managed Agents for server-hosted agents with a managed sandbox, prompt caching, and general Anthropic SDK usage; (4) Claude Tag (Claude in Slack) - what it is, setting it up for a Slack workspace, `/install-slack-app`. **IMPORTANT:** Before spawning a new agent, check if there is already a running or recently completed claude-code-guide agent that you can continue via SendMessage. (Tools: Bash, Read, WebFetch, WebSearch)","- Explore: Read-only search agent for broad fan-out searches — when answering means sweeping many files, directories, or naming conventions and you only need the conclusion, not the file dumps. It reads excerpts rather than whole files, so it locates code; it doesn't review or audit it. Specify search breadth: \"medium\" for moderate exploration, \"very thorough\" for multiple locations and naming conventions. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- general-purpose: General-purpose agent for researching complex questions, searching for code, and executing multi-step tasks. When you are searching for a keyword or file and are not confident that you will find the right match in the first few tries use this agent to perform the search for you. (Tools: *)","- Plan: Software architect agent for designing implementation plans. Use this when you need to plan the implementation strategy for a task. Returns step-by-step plans, identifies critical files, and considers architectural trade-offs. (Tools: All tools except Agent, Artifact, ExitPlanMode, Edit, Write, NotebookEdit)","- statusline-setup: Use this agent to configure the user's Claude Code status line setting. (Tools: Read, Edit)"],"removedTypes":[],"isInitial":true,"showConcurrencyNote":false},"type":"attachment","uuid":"75b0cd0f-23b5-47f0-adf3-cb0e7366a5a3","timestamp":"2026-08-04T10:39:49.486Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.1.219","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"75b0cd0f-23b5-47f0-adf3-cb0e7366a5a3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- agents-sdk: Build AI agents on Cloudflare Workers using the Agents SDK. Load when creating stateful agents, durable workflows, real-time WebSocket apps, scheduled tasks, MCP servers, chat applications, voice agents, or browser automation. Covers Agent class, state management, callable RPC, Workflows, durable execution, queues, retries, observability, and React hooks. Biases towards retrieval from Cloudflare docs over pre-trained knowledge.\n- anime-hardsub-hevc: Depuis un .mkv d'anime fansub (VOSTFR, sous-titres ASS/SSA embarqués), produit une copie qui garde uniquement l'audio japonais, incruste (\"burn\") les sous-titres FR en dur avec une police Anthropic et des pills (fonds arrondis façon Zelda TOTK), et encode en HEVC via le hardware Mac (VideoToolbox / Media Engine). Utiliser quand Matthieu demande de renommer/graver/remuxer/encoder un épisode d'anime avec sous-titres FR incrustés et piste audio JP seule.\n- archive-organize: Ranger, renommer ou déplacer une archive ZenRay DÉJÀ uploadée (manifestes .file.json dans zenray-data) SANS rien re-uploader, en miroir d'une arborescence locale. Aussi : créer une nouvelle archive (archive-folder) avec la convention DJI (date obligatoire, rangé sous Build/DJI/<date>, segments Photos/Videos/BestOf = miroir du dossier source). Utiliser quand Matthieu dit « range / réorganise / renomme / déplace cette archive », « mets l'archive sous tel dossier », « trie l'archive comme sur mon Mac », ou archive un dossier DJI.\n- clean-files-rn-mv: Range, renomme et réorganise des fichiers locaux en vrac (téléchargements, séries/saisons/épisodes, tout dossier aux noms de release torrent sales) en une arborescence propre, SANS JAMAIS écraser, casser ou perdre un fichier. Utiliser dès que Matthieu demande de ranger/trier/renommer/réorganiser des fichiers dans un dossier (Downloads en premier lieu), de nettoyer des noms 