{"parentUuid":"b243191b-7e75-4893-80c1-08bea8c0e2e5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdj49XtHXV91nAf9yY4bq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The Nioh 3 case turns out to be a dead end—it was just a GE-specific regression that got reverted, not an architectural fix I can transpose elsewhere. So there's nothing actually portable from that lead. The real question is why UE videos work on Proton at all, which comes down to how the D3D11 layer functions on Linux.\n\nOn Linux, the DXV K implementation handles NV12 textures properly—the mfplat sample allocator creates real D3D11 NV12 textures and everything works. But on macOS, D3DMetal hangs on that exact same call. This points directly back to my patch T3, which forces the allocator to use CPU memory instead. That's the actual transposable idea, except it came from the measurement, not from Proton. He interrupted me before I could run T3, so I need to report what the research found and ask to proceed with testing it, since the findings now circle back to that specific patch.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_read_input_tokens":350496,"output_tokens":1522,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":350496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1730,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1730},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdj49TVs3R7bnV99M9Uo6","type":"assistant","uuid":"cfe5257d-16af-4f68-89cd-7241efc5c29b","timestamp":"2026-08-05T05:32:59.681Z","effort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","