{"parentUuid":"5ebaae93-d4a0-40f9-b08d-fdd1ff68ddb1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray-Create-Build-Memory/4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e/scratchpad/wv-fork/README.md","snippet":"1\t# winevideo\n2\t\n3\tDrop-in **VP9 / WebM video support for CrossOver 26.2** on Apple Silicon, plus a fix\n4\tfor the d3dmetal crash that kills Media Foundation video playback.\n5\t\n6\tStock CrossOver 26.2 cannot decode VP9 and ships no WebM/Matroska support, so games\n7\tthat play VP9 cutscenes through Windows **Media Foundation** either refuse to start\n8\t(\"the codec needed to play VP9 format videos is not installed\") or hard-crash when a\n9\tframe reaches the GPU. winevideo patches a copy of CrossOver to fix both.\n10\t\n11\tReference test title: **Ninja Gaiden 4** (VP9-in-WebM cutscenes) — boots to gameplay\n12\twith cutscenes playing.\n13\t\n14\t## Screenshots\n15\t\n16\tThe drag-and-drop patcher, and a VP9 cutscene playing in Ninja Gaiden 4 under\n17\tCrossOver 26.2 on the d3dmetal backend:\n18\t\n19\t<p align=\"center\">\n20\t  <img src=\"docs/images/patcher-app.png\" alt=\"winevideo Patcher window\" height=\"340\">\n21\t  &nbsp;&nbsp;\n22\t  <img src=\"docs/images/ng4-cutscene.png\" alt=\"VP9 cutscene playing in Ninja Gaiden 4 under CrossOver 26.2\" height=\"340\">\n23\t</p>\n24\t\n25\t## What it does\n26\t\n27\t1. **Adds a real VP9/VP8 decoder** to CrossOver's GStreamer-backed Media Foundation\n28\t   pipeline (`libgstvpx`) plus WebM/Matroska demuxing (`libgstmatroska`), built against\n29\t   the matching GStreamer 1.24 runtime.\n30\t2. **Advertises VP9 to games.** Registers a real winegstreamer-backed VP9 decoder MFT so\n31\t   `MFTEnumEx(MFT_CATEGORY_VIDEO_DECODER, VP90)` returns it — games gate playback on this\n32\t   check and otherwise show \"VP9 codec not installed.\"\n33\t3. **Fixes the d3dmetal video crash.** On the d3dmetal backend, the D3D11 path cannot\n34\t   create NV12 textures (`CheckFormatSupport(NV12)=0`); Media Foundation creates one\n35\t   anyway and Apple's Metal validation aborts the process (`invalid pixelFormat (0)`).\n36\t   A patched `mfplat` falls back to a supported format (BGRA) instead of crashing. This\n37\t   is codec-independent (it also affected H.264 video).\n38\t4. **Optional: RE Engine and other extra video (WMV/VC-1, …).** If you install the\n39\t   official GStreamer 1.24 framework, the patcher pulls FFmpeg-backed decoders\n40\t   (`libgstlibav`) from *your* install — adding WMV/VC-1/WMA (e.g. Devil May Cry 5 and\n41\t   other Capcom RE Engine logo movies) and more. **Nothing FFmpeg ships in this repo**; it\n42\t   comes from your own GStreamer. See [Extra video codecs](#extra-video-codecs--re-engine-and-more-optional).\n43\t\n44\tSee [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for the full technical breakdown,\n45\t[WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md](WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md) for per-game results, and\n46\t[docs/UE5-ELECTRA-DIAGNOSIS.md](docs/UE5-ELECTRA-DIAGNOSIS.md) for measurement recipes and a\n47\tlist of approaches that were tried and do not work.\n48\t\n49\t## Requirements\n50\t\n51\t- **CrossOver 26.2** (the stable release — **not** CrossOver Preview), Apple Silicon\n52\t  (macOS). The binaries are built against 26.2's Wine 11.0 / GStreamer 1.24.5 and are\n53\t  version-specific; the patcher refuses other builds.\n54\t- Use the **d3dmetal** graphics backend (the only one that runs most D3D12 titles).\n55\t- Also reported working on **CrossOver 26.3** (Wine 11.0 too): the patcher's guard checks for\n56\t  `lib64/gstreamer-1.0` rather than the version string, and it applies cleanly. See\n57\t  [WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md](WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md).\n58\t\n59\t## Install\n60\t\n61\tPatch a **copy** of CrossOver — never the original.\n62\t\n63\t### GUI\n64\t\n65\tOpen `gui/winevideo Patcher.app`:\n66\t\n67\t1. Drag your `CrossOver.app` onto the window — it copies it to\n68\t   `~/Applications/CrossOver-winevideo.app` (a copy only — nothing is patched yet).\n69\t2. Click **Scan bottles** and tick the bottle you play your VP9 game (e.g. Ninja Gaiden 4)\n70\t   in. Games gate on the VP9 decoder MFT, which is registered *per bottle* — so the bottle\n71\t   you play in must be patched, not just the app.\n72\t3. Click **Patch**. This patches the app **and** the selected bottle(s) in one step — no\n73\t   password or special permissions required.\n74\t4. Launch `~/Applications/CrossOver-winevideo.app` and run the game.\n75\t\n76\tThe app is unsigned; clear quarantine before first launch:\n77\t`xattr -cr \"gui/winevideo Patcher.app\"`.\n78\t\n79\t### Command line\n80\t\n81\t```sh\n82\t# duplicate first (Finder, or: ditto /Applications/CrossOver.app ~/Applications/CrossOver-winevideo.app)\n83\tpatcher/patch.sh /path/to/CrossOver-copy.app [bottle ...]\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\t- No bottle argument → patches the app and every existing bottle.\n87\t- The app-level DLLs apply to all bottles; the per-bottle registry must be applied to\n88\t  each bottle (re-run with a bottle name for bottles created later).\n89\t\n90\tRevert with `patcher/restore.sh /path/to/CrossOver-copy.app [bottle ...]`.\n91\t\n92\t## Extra video codecs — RE Engine and more (optional)\n93\t\n94\tSome games — Capcom **RE Engine** titles (**Devil May Cry 5**, RE2/3/8, MHW) and others —\n95\tplay movies in formats CrossOver and Apple's VideoToolbox can't decode (notably\n96\t**WMV9 / VC-1**), and crash on the missing decoder. These need FFmpeg-backed decoders.\n97\t\n98\tTo keep this project free of redistributed codecs, **winevideo does not ship FFmpeg** — it\n99\tuses the decoders from *your own* GStreamer install:\n100\t\n101\t1. Install the official **GStreamer 1.24.13** runtime framework (default install):\n102\t   <https://gstreamer.freedesktop.org/data/pkg/osx/1.24.13/gstreamer-1.0-1.24.13-universal.pkg>\n103\t   It **must be 1.24.x** — newer 1.26/1.28 builds use a glib that won't load in CrossOver's\n104\t   glib 2.78; the patcher version-checks and refuses cleanly rather than break.\n105\t2. Patch as usual (GUI or CLI). The patcher detects your GStreamer framework, pulls\n106\t   `libgstlibav` (+ its FFmpeg libraries) from it, thins them to x86_64 and adapts them into\n107\t   the patched CrossOver, and reports `RE Engine codecs added from your GStreamer ✓`.\n108\t3. If GStreamer isn't installed, this step is **skipped** — VP9 / Ninja Gaiden 4 still works\n109\t   with no extra download. Only the FFmpeg-backed codecs require the GStreamer install.\n110\t\n111\tThis gives `avdec_vc1` / `avdec_wmv3` / `avdec_wmav2` (WMV/VC-1/WMA) plus H.264/AAC/AC-3, so\n112\tRE Engine movies play. The codec binaries are the GStreamer Foundation's, taken from your\n113\tmachine at patch time — this repo redistributes none of them.\n114\t\n115\t## How a patched app is produced\n116\t\n117\tThe patcher copies prebuilt artifacts (`patcher/payload/`) into the app, ad-hoc signs the\n118\tadded libraries, registers the VP9 decoder MFT and `.webm`/`.mkv`/`.msd` byte-stream\n119\thandlers in the bottle registry, then re-seals the bundle. To avoid needing an admin\n120\tpassword or Full Disk Access, it stages the copy as a plain **folder** (macOS App\n121\tManagement only guards real `.app` bundles), patches and re-seals it there as the normal\n122\tuser, then renames it to `.app`. The macOS-specific steps (copy with `ditto`, strip\n123\tquarantine, ad-hoc re-seal **without** `--deep` to preserve Wine's entitlements, and wait\n124\tfor Wine's registry flush) are documented in [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).\n125\t\n126\t## Repository layout\n127\t\n128\t| Path | Contents |\n129\t|------|----------|\n130\t| `patcher/` | Self-contained patcher: `patch.sh`, `restore.sh`, and `payload/` (prebuilt DLLs/plugins/deps + registry) |\n131\t| `gui/` | SwiftUI front-end (`WineVideoPatcher.swift`) and `build-app.sh` |\n132\t| `build/` | Scripts and patches to rebuild the Wine DLLs from CrossOver 26.2 source |\n133\t| `build/patches/` | Wine source patches (VP9/AV1 caps, VP9 decoder MFT, mfplat BGRA fallback, build guards) |\n134\t| `docs/` | Architecture and technical notes |\n135\t| `mf_probe*.c`, `mft_probe.c` | Standalone test harnesses (decode probe, MFT-enumeration probe, D3D-backed probes) |\n136\t\n137\t## Building from source\n138\t\n139\tThe payload is prebuilt, so rebuilding is only needed to modify the Wine DLLs. See\n140\t[build/README.md](build/README.md). The Wine source patches are in `build/patches/`.\n141\t\n142\t## Scope and limitations\n143\t\n144\t- Covers games that play video through **Windows Media Foundation** (`IMFSourceReader`),\n145\t  the common path for non-Unreal titles.\n\n... [79 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c99616be-bded-42a3-9638-6ebc5e97b547","timestamp":"2026-08-05T13:00:09.283Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
