{"parentUuid":"c160201f-bc93-4bd4-ada9-4fdace759d8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdjeJX8r2fih1X4uaHEv3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TK9XCrK8jZEbRviaFEZBqZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray-Create-Build-Memory/4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e/scratchpad/wv-fork; cd \"$S\" && gh pr create --repo Jfishin/winevideo --base main --head matthieuhuguet:beast-of-reincarnation-and-electra-notes --title \"Beast of Reincarnation (UE5/Electra) works: results, the Engine.ini read-only trap, and diagnosis notes\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nThanks for this project. It fixed a title I had spent a full night failing to fix on my own, so here is everything I learned, given back.\n\n**Beast of Reincarnation** (Unreal Engine 5.4.4, ElectraPlayer, H.264 1080p + AAC 5.1, cooked D3D12/SM6 only) now plays every cutscene end to end, on **CrossOver 26.3**, `d3dmetal` backend, Apple GPTK 4.0 beta 2, with GStreamer 1.24.13 installed so the FFmpeg decoders were pulled in too. Measured rather than eyeballed: `read_transform_output_video` fires hundreds of times per scene, no crash, progression unblocked.\n\nThree additions.\n\n**1. The `Engine.ini` read-only trap (README).** This one cost me a scare and I suspect it costs you users. Unreal rewrites `Saved/Config/Windows` and can delete an `Engine.ini` it did not create. The failure mode is genuinely confusing: the first cutscene plays perfectly, then the file is gone, and the *next* launch crashes back on the NV12 texture path. It reads exactly like an unstable patch, and my first reaction was that the install had broken something. `chmod 444` on the file after creating it removes the problem entirely.\n\n**2. CrossOver 26.3 (README + new `WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md`).** The patcher applies cleanly to 26.3 as well as 26.2. Reading `patch.sh`, the guard tests for `lib64/gstreamer-1.0` rather than the version string, which is why it passes. `patch.sh` already pointed at `WORKING-AND-BROKEN-GAMES.md`, so this creates the file with the two known-working titles and the exact per-game recipe. Adjust or drop it if you had a different shape in mind.\n\n**3. `docs/UE5-ELECTRA-DIAGNOSIS.md`.** Field notes from a debugging session that happened *before* I found winevideo and that independently reached the same root cause, `DXGI_FORMAT_NV12` (103) being unsupported by the D3D11-to-Metal layer. It contains the measured Media Foundation call chain, a few reproducible measurement recipes, and a table of **thirteen approaches that were tried and do not work**, each with what was actually measured.\n\nThat last table is the part I think matters most here. Your README states the project is AI-generated and AI-assisted; an agent that reads only the fix will happily re-explore every one of those dead ends, several of which look extremely promising on paper. A couple of them are traps worth knowing regardless: the `+mfplat` Wine debug channel freezes the game by itself, so it silently invalidates any liveness measurement, and CrossOver's *Run with Options* pushes environment variables into the Windows environment, where GStreamer, running on the macOS side, never sees them.\n\nHappy to split this into smaller PRs, reword anything, or move the notes wherever you prefer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open the pull request"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_read_input_tokens":566890,"output_tokens":1313,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":566890,"cac