même essayer.\n\n**Le patch 7 résout mon plantage**, celui du fil `ElectraPlayer::Video decoder`. Leur commentaire est limpide : les buffers de l'allocateur implémentent **`IMF2DBuffer`**, « ce que des consommateurs comme UE Electra exigent sur les images vidéo ; un simple buffer mémoire fourni par l'appelant ne l'implémente pas, si bien qu'ils rejettent chaque image ». C'était précisément mon `QueryInterface` sur l'IID `a06eb39a` qui renvoyait zéro.\n\n**Autrement dit, chacune de mes impasses était une moitié du vrai correctif.** J'avais bon sur le diagnostic et faux sur la couche où agir.\n\nJe corrige la branche, parce qu'elle porte la même erreur d'attribution que mon explication."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1675,"cache_read_input_tokens":581830,"output_tokens":3689,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1675,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3689,"cache_read_input_tokens":581830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1675},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdjg5aJxjG3TKRHJhBaUt","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d367565-7b0b-4d0a-bf03-96cff4f77efc","timestamp":"2026-08-05T13:24:33.212Z","effort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"6d367565-7b0b-4d0a-bf03-96cff4f77efc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cdjg5gu6LpRtGLmFt1cAn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014xcW2uC6AwyJ8SggSdAqZs","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray-Create-Build-Memory/4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e/scratchpad/wv-fork/docs/UE5-ELECTRA-DIAGNOSIS.md","old_string":"## 5. What actually works\n\nThe two pieces this project provides, and they are both required:\n\n1. The patched `mfplat` NV12 → BGRA fallback, which stops Media Foundation from asking the\n   graphics layer for a texture format it reports as unsupported.\n2. The per-game `Engine.ini` with `Electra.Win.H264UseOldOutputPath=1`, which makes Electra\n   take its CPU output path and stop requesting a GPU texture in the first place.","new_string":"## 5. Which patches actually carry an Electra title\n\nWorth spelling out, because the obvious guess is wrong. For an H.264/Electra title the\n`mfplat` NV12 → BGRA fallback (`0004`) is a safety net that may never even fire: once\n`0005` refuses the D3D device manager, no D3D texture is ever allocated. The two patches\nthat carry the title are `0005` and `0007`, with `0006` cleaning up the audio track.\n\n| Patch | File | Effect on an Electra title |\n|---|---|---|\n| `0002`, `0003` | `wg_media_type.c`, `video_decoder.c` | VP9 only, not involved. |\n| `0004` | `mfplat/sample.c` | Safety net for the `IMFSourceReader` path. Not the mechanism here. |\n| **`0005`** | `winegstreamer/video_decoder.c` | **Decisive.** Three changes: NV12 becomes enumerable again *only when no D3D manager is set* (narrowing CW HACK 26265); `MFT_MESSAGE_SET_D3D_MANAGER` returns `E_NOTIMPL` on macOS; `MF_SA_D3D_AWARE` / `MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE` are advertised as FALSE on macOS. Electra therefore takes its software path from the start. |\n| **`0007`** | `winegstreamer/video_decoder.c` | **Decisive.** Sets `MFT_OUTPUT_STREAM_PROVIDES_SAMPLES` on macOS so the decoder supplies its own samples, whose buffers implement `IMF2DBuffer`. Electra requires that interface on video frames and silently rejects every frame without it. |\n| **`0006`** | `winegstreamer/wg_format.c` | Fixes the AAC `codec_data` double strip, i.e. the `Need codec_data for raw AAC` error above. |\n\nRead against that table, every dead end in section 4 is **half of the real fix applied at\nthe wrong layer**. Hand-clearing the NV12 skip is `0005` without its two other changes, so\nNV12 also becomes available on the D3D path and the game hangs. Neutralising\n`sample_allocator_SetDirectXManager` in `mfplat` is `0005`'s `E_NOTIMPL` one layer too low,\nand without `0007` the resulting plain memory buffers have no `IMF2DBuffer`, which is\nexactly the `QueryInterface` returning `NULL` in the crash of dead end 3.\n\nPlus the per-game `Engine.ini` with `Electra.Win.H264UseOldOutputPath=1`, which puts Electra\non its CPU output path."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1675,"cache_read_input_tokens":581830,"output_tokens":3689,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1675,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3689,"cache_read_input_tokens":581830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1675},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdjg5aJxjG3TKRHJhBaUt","type":"assistant","uuid":"d3c4590a-fea8-410a-a281-3db04f4b9f54","timestamp":"2026-08-05T13:24:48.418Z","effort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.