{"parentUuid":"3f77564b-495c-48fe-8679-c8516cac1cd4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-zenray-Create-Build-Memory/4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e/scratchpad/wv-fork/docs/UE5-ELECTRA-DIAGNOSIS.md","snippet":"1\t# UE5 / ElectraPlayer on CrossOver — diagnosis notes and dead ends\n2\t\n3\tField notes from a full debugging session on **Beast of Reincarnation** (Unreal Engine\n4\t5.4.4, cooked D3D12/SM6 only) on macOS 27, Apple M5 Max, CrossOver 26.3, `d3dmetal`\n5\tbackend with Apple GPTK 4.0 beta 2.\n6\t\n7\tThe session happened **before** winevideo was found, and independently arrived at the\n8\tsame root cause this project fixes. It is written down here because the project is\n9\tAI-generated and AI-assisted: an agent that reads only the fix will happily re-explore\n10\tevery dead end listed below. Each one was measured, not guessed, and each one cost real\n11\ttime.\n12\t\n13\tEverything below is reproducible on a stock CrossOver install.\n14\t\n15\t---\n16\t\n17\t## 1. Symptom\n18\t\n19\t3D, menus and gameplay run perfectly. Cutscenes play as a **black screen with no audio**,\n20\tthe game does not crash, and progression is blocked because the story gates on them.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## 2. The chain, as measured\n25\t\n26\tThe game imports `MF.dll`, `MFPlat.dll`, `MFReadWrite.dll` and ships ElectraPlayer\n27\t(threads `ElectraPlayer::MP4 streamer`, `::Video decoder`, `::Audio decoder`).\n28\t\n29\tTraced with `cxstart --debugmsg \"+mfplat\" --cx-log <file>`:\n30\t\n31\t- `MFTEnumEx(MFT_CATEGORY_VIDEO_DECODER, MFVideoFormat_H264)` → Wine's `h264_decoder`.\n32\t- Video: H.264 1920x1080 @ 29.97 fps. Audio: AAC 5.1 48 kHz.\n33\t- Unreal creates an `IMFDXGIDeviceManager`, calls `MFCreateVideoSampleAllocatorEx`,\n34\t  `sample_allocator_SetDirectXManager`, then `InitializeSampleAllocatorEx(10, 10)` with an\n35\t  **NV12** media type, then `dxgi_device_manager_OpenDeviceHandle`,\n36\t  `GetVideoService(ID3D11Device)`, `MFCreateTrackedSample`.\n37\t- The bottle's `system32/d3d11.dll` is **Wine's own** (425 552 bytes), not DXMT's and not\n38\t  DXVK's, so on `d3dmetal` the D3D11 video device is Wine d3d11 backed by D3DMetal.\n39\t\n40\tTwo independent walls follow.\n41\t\n42\t**Wall 1 — Wine never offers NV12.** `transform_GetOutputAvailableType` in\n43\t`winegstreamer.dll` skips it explicitly (`Skipping NV12 output format`). Unmodified, the\n44\tgame therefore negotiates **I420** and shows nothing. On CrossOver 26.3 the skip is a\n45\t`je +0x20` (`74 20`) at RVA `0x2c6be`.\n46\t\n47\t**Wall 2 — no graphics layer can create the texture.** With NV12 unblocked:\n48\t\n49\t| Backend | Behaviour |\n50\t|---|---|\n51\t| `dxmt` | `CreateMTLTextureDescriptorInternal: creating a texture of invalid format: 103` (103 = `DXGI_FORMAT_NV12`), twenty times per playback. DXMT's `d3d11.dll` contains **zero** occurrences of `PlaneSlice`, so it has no planar texture support at all. |\n52\t| `d3dmetal` | No graphics error at all, but the process hangs forever right after `MFCreateTrackedSample`, CPU falls to 0 %. |\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t## 3. Useful measurement tricks\n57\t\n58\t**Tell \"waiting\" from \"rendering\" without looking at the screen.** A hung Electra playback\n59\tsits at ~0 % CPU; a healthy game sits at 100–400 %. `ps -o %cpu= -p <pid>` sampled twice,\n60\t8 s apart, is enough to classify a black screen without asking a human.\n61\t\n62\t**Get the engine's own fatal error out of a shipping build.** Shipping UE builds strip\n63\tlogging, but `LowLevelFatalError` still goes through `OutputDebugString`. Running with\n64\t`--debugmsg \"+seh\"` and grepping the log for `OutputDebugString` reconstructs it, including\n65\tthe crashing thread name.\n66\t\n67\t**Do not measure liveness with `+mfplat` enabled.** That channel writes millions of lines\n68\tand freezes the game **by itself**, including on a completely stock install. Several early\n69\t\"it hangs\" conclusions in this session were artefacts of the tracer, not of the change\n70\tunder test. Use `GST_DEBUG=1` or `2` instead, which is cheap.\n71\t\n72\t**Watch frames actually being handed over.** With `GST_DEBUG=2`, a working playback prints\n73\t`wg_transform.c:read_transform_output_video: Copied 3133440 bytes` once per frame\n74\t(1920x1088 NV12). Zero of those lines means the problem is upstream of the handover; many\n75\tof them with a black screen means it is downstream.\n76\t\n77\t**DXMT has a debug log**: `DXMT_LOG_LEVEL=debug`. D3DMetal has `D3DM_LOGLEVEL_INFO=1` and\n78\t`D3DM_NOT_IMPLEMENTED=1`. Both write to the process stderr, so redirect the launcher.\n79\t\n80\t**Environment variables must be set on the Unix side.** CrossOver's *Run with Options* and\n81\t`cxstart --env` push variables into the **Windows** environment; GStreamer runs on the macOS\n82\tside and never sees them. `export` before launching the shortcut instead. A silent, empty\n83\t`GST_DEBUG_FILE` is the tell.\n84\t\n85\t---\n86\t\n87\t## 4. Dead ends — do not re-explore\n88\t\n89\tAll of these were tried and measured on the setup above. None makes the picture appear.\n90\t\n91\t| # | Attempt | Measured result |\n92\t|---|---|---|\n93\t| 1 | Patch out the NV12 skip in `winegstreamer` (2 bytes at RVA `0x2c6be`) | NV12 is negotiated, then the game hangs at 0 % CPU before reaching the menus. Necessary but far from sufficient. |\n94\t| 2 | Reorder `h264_decoder_output_types` (RVA `0x4d4e0`) to put YUY2 first | Unreal enumerates the whole list and picks NV12 regardless. Format order is not a lever. |\n95\t| 3 | Neutralise `sample_allocator_SetDirectXManager` in `mfplat` (3 bytes at RVA `0x281e0`, `xor eax,eax; ret`) to force system-memory buffers | Game starts, then crashes in thread `ElectraPlayer::Video decoder`, `EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION` reading `0x0`. Disassembly shows a `QueryInterface` for IID `a06eb39a-50da-425b-8c31-4eecd6c270f3` whose HRESULT is **not checked** before the pointer is dereferenced. Patch `0007` explains it: Electra requires `IMF2DBuffer` on video frames, and a plain caller-provided memory buffer does not implement it. |\n96\t| 4 | `-dx11` on the command line | No effect; the title is cooked SM6 only. |\n97\t| 5 | Disable Media Foundation entirely (`WINEDLLOVERRIDES` for `mfplat,mf,mfreadwrite,winegstreamer`) | No effect on the black screen. |\n98\t| 6 | User `Game.ini` clearing `StartupMovies` | No effect. |\n99\t| 7 | `sg.ResolutionQuality` 0 → 100 | No effect. |\n100\t| 8 | `CX_GRAPHICS_BACKEND=dxvk` | Game crashes at startup: DXVK provides D3D9–11 only, the title is D3D12. |\n101\t| 9 | Hybrid: DXVK's `d3d11.dll` copied into the bottle while D3D12 stays on D3DMetal | Game runs, picture still black. |\n102\t| 10 | Official GStreamer + `GST_PLUGIN_PATH` alone | Every plugin is rejected: `has incompatible version (plugin: 1.28, gst: 1.24)`. |\n103\t| 11 | Same, plus `DYLD_LIBRARY_PATH` at the framework so the 1.28 **core** loads too | Plugins load (0 rejections, confirmed by the `aacparse` error moving from `gstaacparse.c:358` to `:355`), `avdec_h264`/`avdec_aac` available and ranked MAX. Picture still black. |\n104\t| 12 | Rank `aacparse:NONE` to bypass the AAC parser | `Need codec_data for raw AAC` disappears, Wine can no longer build the audio transform at all, picture still black. **Audio is not the blocker.** |\n105\t| 13 | Homebrew `gst-libav` | Unusable: CrossOver's Wine runs **x86_64**, Homebrew on Apple Silicon ships **arm64**. `dlopen` fails with `incompatible architecture`. Only the official universal package works. |\n106\t\n107\tTwo side observations worth keeping:\n108\t\n109\t- The AAC media type carries only **12 bytes** of `MF_MT_USER_DATA`, i.e. the `HEAACWAVEINFO`\n110\t  struct with no `AudioSpecificConfig` after it, which is why `aacparse` legitimately\n111\t  refuses with `Need codec_data for raw AAC`. It is noisy but harmless.\n112\t- Wiping `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\<Project>\\Saved` (config + `PCD3D_SM6` pipeline cache) cured an\n113\t  unrelated hard boot crash. Worth trying before blaming anything else, but keep\n114\t  `SaveGames` aside first.\n115\t\n116\t---\n117\t\n118\t## 5. Which patches actually carry an Electra title\n119\t\n120\tWorth spelling out, because the obvious guess is wrong. For an H.264/Electra title the\n121\t`mfplat` NV12 → BGRA fallback (`0004`) is a safety net that may never even fire: once\n122\t`0005` refuses the D3D device manager, no D3D texture is ever allocated. The two patches\n123\tthat carry the title are `0005` and `0007`, with `0006` cleaning up the audio track.\n124\t\n125\t| Patch | File | Effect on an Electra title |\n126\t|---|---|---|\n\n... [23 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fc79fbb4-be15-4998-a6e1-599b55aafaa7","timestamp":"2026-08-05T13:25:10.030Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"fc79fbb4-be15-4998-a6e1-599b55aafaa7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CdjgBDLZfK2NRtq166Rf2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**La branche est corrigée et la pull request mise à jour.** Voici ce que j'ai dû rectifier, et c'est une vraie erreur de ma part.\n\n## Ce que je t'avais mal dit\n\nJ'avais présenté le patch 4, le repli NV12 vers BGRA, comme « le » correctif. C'est faux pour ton jeu. Sur un titre Electra, **ce patch ne se déclenche probablement jamais**, puisque le patch 5 refuse l'appareil Direct3D avant même qu'une texture soit demandée. Il ne sert que pour l'autre famille de jeux, ceux qui passent par `IMFSourceReader`.\n\n## Qui fait quoi, vraiment\n\n**Le patch 5, `winegstreamer/video_decoder.c`, fait trois choses.** Il rend NV12 de nouveau proposable, mais **seulement quand aucun appareil Direct3D n'est en jeu**. Il répond `E_NOTIMPL` quand Unreal tend son gestionnaire Direct3D. Et il déclare `MF_SA_D3D11_AWARE = FALSE` sur macOS, si bien qu'Unreal part directement sur sa voie logicielle.\n\n**Le patch 7, même fichier**, ajoute `MFT_OUTPUT_STREAM_PROVIDES_SAMPLES` sur macOS : le décodeur fournit ses propres échantillons, dont les buffers implémentent **`IMF2DBuffer`**. Leur commentaire dit qu'Electra exige cette interface sur les images et rejette silencieusement toutes celles qui ne l'ont pas.\n\n**Le patch 6, `wg_format.c`**, répare le `codec_data` AAC, c'est-à-dire exactement l'erreur `Need codec_data for raw AAC` que nous avions mesurée.\n\n## Le point qui rend tout limpide\n\n**Chacune de mes impasses était la moitié du vrai correctif, appliquée une couche trop bas.**\n\nMon déblocage NV12 à deux octets, c'était le patch 5 amputé de ses deux autres changements, donc NV12 devenait disponible aussi sur la voie Direct3D, et le jeu se figeait.\n\nMa neutralisation de `SetDirectXManager`, c'était le `E_NOTIMPL` du patch 5, mais posé dans `mfplat` au lieu du décodeur. Et sans le patch 7, les buffers obtenus n'avaient pas `IMF2DBuffer`, ce qui **est** exactement le `QueryInterface` renvoyant zéro dans mon plantage.\n\nL'IID mystérieux `a06eb39a` que je n'avais pas su identifier, c'était donc ça.\n\nCes trois explications sont maintenant dans le document de la branche, avec un tableau patch par patch et le lien explicite entre chaque impasse et le patch qui la supersède. La pull request est à jour : **https://github.com/Jfishin/winevideo/pull/1**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5235,"cache_read_input_tokens":587323,"output_tokens":1029,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5235,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1029,"cache_read_input_tokens":587323,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdjgB5vL5Wb6RWt7HkBo7","type":"assistant","uuid":"0975f728-5058-49d0-aa17-fd697a2bf134","timestamp":"2026-08-05T13:25:28.963Z","effort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"4d7c85c8-de5a-48bd-af30-1bf0bd2b590e","version":"2.1.221","gitBranch":"main"}
